.TH CHTTPSVR_REQ_PARAM 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_req_param \- look up a named path parameter
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

const char *chttpsvr_req_param(const chttpsvr_req *req,
                                const char *name);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns the URL-decoded value of the path parameter called name.  If
the route pattern that matched has no parameter with that name, the
result is NULL.

A parameter captures one raw path segment and that segment is decoded
separately, so the value can hold a '/' that arrived as %2F and it can
also be "." or "..".  Never use it as a file name without checking
it first.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_req_path (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_query (3)
